; QSSC P1 -- PIN-SCAFFOLD SUPPORT: 8x8 circle-bored hole grid for PCB pin headers
; GENERATED by tools/gen_qssc_gcode.py -- deterministic, auditable
; Stock: 20x20x3 mm FR4 (or clear acrylic) | tool: 1.0 mm flat end-mill
; spindle 8000 rpm | bore feed 100 mm/min | through Z-3.0
; PINS: standard 2.54 mm pitch male pin header, 0.64 mm square, tin-plated
;   (Mill-Max 1129 / Harwin M50 machined round gold pins = the upgrade for uniform coating).
; 8x8 = 64 holes @ 2.54 mm pitch, centred (first pin 1.11 mm), 1.5 mm dia.
; 1 mm bit CIRCLE-BORES 1.5 mm holes (linear-segment polygon circles, visible in a top view) -> 0.43 mm radial clearance (0.64 mm pin).
; NOT a Z-only peck drill (invisible as a point) and NOT G02 arcs (some viewers misdraw I/J as a diagonal) -- a real polygon circle per hole.
; DETECTOR: paste-mold graphene then MoS2+PEDOT:PSS around each pin in the hole;
;   ITO glass under the support = common back-electrode (DET_COMMON).
; EMITTER: paste-mold ZnO then CQD then PEDOT:PSS around each pin -- symmetric
;   to the detector; pin = cathode, ITO glass under the support = EM_ANODE anode.
; COORDS: support-local. WORK ZERO = support bottom-left (0,0). 20x20 overlays the P0 die.

G21 G90 G94 G17 G40 G49 G80   ; mm, abs, feed/min, XY plane, cancel comp
G0 Z10.0                       ; safe Z FIRST
M03 S8000                    ; spindle ON only after Z is safe

; -- support bounding box (engrave, visual frame) --
G0 X0.000 Y0.000
G1 Z-0.100 F100
G1 X20.000 Y0.000 F100
G1 X20.000 Y20.000 F100
G1 X0.000 Y20.000 F100
G1 X0.000 Y0.000 F100
G0 Z10.000
; -- corner fiducials (registration) --
